<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47533" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠρεμ-έω</span></b> , hyperdor. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρεμ-</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Ti.Locr.
			95d
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be still,
				keep quiet, be at rest</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κινέομαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				238b23
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				p.12
			</span></i> M.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἠρεμοῦν</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κινούμενον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				986a24
			</span></i>; of the object of knowledge, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				96b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				100a6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς νόμοις ἠρεμοῦντες διαμένειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					7.3
				</span></i>
			; <i>acquiesce</i> in a verdict, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				956d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. τῇ διανοίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					2.21.22
				</span></i>
			: acc. to Stoics, only of animate beings, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.161
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be unmoved, remain fixed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόνος οὗτος ἠ. ὁ λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					527b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				891a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c.
			inf., <i>refrain from</i> doing . . , <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Jud.Voc.</u>
				4
			</span></i> (s.v.l.).</div>
